WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.299 --> 00:00:05.700
Extremities is back and better than ever,
but it’s going to be different.

00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:10.250
Much has changed since the last season of
the Extremities podcast.

00:00:10.250 --> 00:00:15.550
Travel screeched to a halt, and with this
standstill went my ability to visit, document,

00:00:15.550 --> 00:00:18.109
and share the stories of far-away places.

00:00:18.109 --> 00:00:23.689
Yet, through all the changes and tumult brought
on by the last 18 months, some things stayed

00:00:23.689 --> 00:00:28.829
quite the same—principally, telling stories
of the world’s most remote settlements remained

00:00:28.829 --> 00:00:30.539
a core interest of mine.

00:00:30.539 --> 00:00:36.510
And so, while serving the same purpose—to
access and explain the isolated and difficult-to-comprehend

00:00:36.510 --> 00:00:42.719
corners of the globe—Extremities is returning,
but in a new form… and this time you’re

00:00:42.719 --> 00:00:44.460
going to need a screen.

00:00:44.460 --> 00:00:48.329
Extremities is relaunching as a standalone
YouTube channel.

00:00:48.329 --> 00:00:52.510
For those of you curious as to how a civil
war influences one of the most biodiverse

00:00:52.510 --> 00:00:57.780
islands on the planet, how French culture
perpetuates in the subantarctic, or why centuries-old

00:00:57.780 --> 00:01:02.749
Atlantic island communities have been all-but-abandoned
over the course of just a few decades, come

00:01:02.749 --> 00:01:06.750
on over to the Extremities channel right now
and give it a watch.

00:01:06.750 --> 00:01:10.970
The first two videos are up now; the third
will go up in a week, or it’s on Nebula

00:01:10.970 --> 00:01:15.210
now; and then more will go out every third
Wednesday after that.

00:01:15.210 --> 00:01:19.940
Each video features interviews with locals
and experts alike—taking you to the place,

00:01:19.940 --> 00:01:23.720
introducing you to its people, and telling
its story.

00:01:23.720 --> 00:01:28.040
Ad-free episodes along with extended cuts
of interviews will also be available for Nebula

00:01:28.040 --> 00:01:29.040
subscribers.

00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:33.120
So, head to this link, clickable at the top
of the description, to watch and subscribe

00:01:33.120 --> 00:01:35.590
to Wendover Productions’ newest channel.

